# Browser extensions (extensions/)

- `qe-consultancy-chrome/` and `qe-consultancy-safari/` hold the **same** extension. The root JS, CSS, HTML and JSON files (`content.js`, `background.js`, `bridge.js`, `field-map.js`, `is-code-fetch.js`, `popup.*`, `block-rules.json`, `manifest.json`, ...) are mirrored. Change both copies in the same edit.
- When behaviour changes, bump `"version"` in **both** `manifest.json` files and in `extensions/README.md` (currently 2.2.32).
- `qe-consultancy-safari/macos-generated/` is generated by `convert-with-xcode.sh`. Don't hand-edit it; regenerate it. The hand-maintained Xcode wrapper is `qe-consultancy-safari/macos/`. Chrome's `_metadata/` is generated too.
- No secrets or API keys in the extension. The app passes `returnUrl` at runtime. Manak PDFs upload to the functions service at `/api/osl/manak-pdf`.
- Allowed app origins (localhost, `*.qengineering.in`, `*.up.railway.app`) are listed in the README. Keep the manifest and README consistent when you change them.
- Portal content scripts target `manakonline.in`, `lims.bis.gov.in`, `standards.bis.gov.in` and `standardsbis.bsbedge.com`. Keep selectors defensive, because portal markup changes.
